       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum daily dose. I know of no indication that supports it, and it carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Normal kidney and liver function and no allergies don't lower that risk enough.\n\nYou can still get this patient treated:\n- **Enter a dose within limits.** I can enter 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3200 mg/day) or a lower dose right away.\n- **Talk to pharmacy first.** If you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, a pharmacist or the attending can review it. If they approve a nonstandard dose, it can go through the hospital's override process with the rationale documented.\n- **Consider other options.** If pain or inflammation control is the goal, I can enter an adjunct such as acetaminophen, or you can pick another agent.\n\nWhich would you like me to do?"
